%% seam — the kit's main boundary: deterministic observation vs. model inference,
%% with the human audit as the trust flip. Drafted [inferred] 2026-07-02;
%% regenerate via /cold-start rather than hand-editing.
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as Human
    participant K as Kit CLI (deterministic)
    participant A as AI agent (inference)
    participant R as ai/ knowledge layer

    U->>K: shazam <repo>
    K->>R: repo-profile.json · scaffolds · install-manifest.json
    Note over K,R: facts only — no LLM, nothing executed

    U->>A: /cold-start
    A->>R: draft MODULE_MAP / ARCHITECTURE / FEATURE_MAP …
    Note over A,R: everything tagged [inferred]

    U->>R: audit (~30 min): set Stability, flip [inferred] → [verified] (date)
    Note over U,R: the flip is the human's signature — agents never do it

    loop keep it honest (CI + on demand)
        K->>R: verify --strict (path claims) · drift --git --strict (map decay)
    end

    U->>A: /add-feature (agent now navigates via the verified map)
